Port Mesa to LikeOS: a POSIX system with no KMS/DRM anywhere.

Six changes, one theme -- the "software rasterizer only, no DRM, X11 via
the drisw winsys" configuration had never been link-tested as a whole:

 - util/detect_os.h, util/os_misc.c: DETECT_OS_LIKEOS, declared POSIX; the
   os_misc include ladder accepts it (the sysconf paths do the real work).
 - include/drm-uapi/drm.h: a platform branch that takes the ioctl request
   macros from <sys/ioctl.h>; the header must parse even where no DRM
   device can ever exist, because it defines types shared with code that
   also runs where one does.
 - gallium/frontends/dri/dri2_stubs.c (new) + meson.build: dri2.c is only
   compiled with a DRM display system, but libEGL and libGL reference its
   PUBLIC entry points unconditionally.  The stubs answer "unsupported" in
   each interface's own vocabulary -- the same pattern kopper_stubs.c
   already uses for a build without the vulkan swrast.
 - meson.build: link xxf86vm for GLX on dri platform 'none' too, not only
   'drm' -- glxcmds.c compiles the same VidMode calls on both.
 - glx/glx_pbuffer.c: the dri3 buffer-age query behind HAVE_DRI3; without
   DRI3 a GLX_DRIVER_DRI3 display cannot exist, so the branch is dead
   there anyway -- but it must not be a link error.

--- a/src/util/detect_os.h
+++ b/src/util/detect_os.h
@@ -91,6 +91,14 @@
 #define DETECT_OS_POSIX 1
 #endif
 
+#if defined(__LIKEOS__)
+/* LikeOS: a POSIX system without KMS/DRM.  Every driver here is software
+ * (llvmpipe/softpipe over the drisw winsys), so the generic POSIX paths are
+ * exactly right and nothing OS-specific is wanted. */
+#define DETECT_OS_LIKEOS 1
+#define DETECT_OS_POSIX 1
+#endif
+
 
